      "content": "Getting Started with CloudScale API\n\nTo begin using the CloudScale API, start by generating an API key in the CloudScale dashboard. This key will be used to authenticate your requests.\n\nOnce you have your API key, you can obtain a Bearer token by calling the `/auth/login` endpoint. You'll need to pass your client ID and secret in the request body.\n\nHere's an example of how to authenticate using the `curl` command:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \\\n  https://api.cloudscale.io/auth/login \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"client_id\": \"your_client_id\", \"secret\": \"your_client_secret\"}'\n```\nReplace `your_client_id` and `your_client_secret` with the values from your CloudScale dashboard.\n\nAfter obtaining your Bearer token, you can make API requests to the CloudScale endpoint using the token in the `Authorization` header. For example:\n```bash\ncurl -X GET \\\n  https://api.cloudscale.io/endpoint \\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_bearer_token'\n```\nNote that the CloudScale API has a rate limit of 1000 requests per minute. Be mindful of this limit when",
